{"version":"1","id":"thorstenhans","handle":"thorstenhans","name":"Thorsten Hans","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/ffdd8d9ab69947edb960cdcd6c39e9b2","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-6.9421,"y":-3.7813,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":20,"newest_post_at":"2025-10-16T14:50:52.855Z","oldest_post_at":"2023-05-18T11:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":3.2,"summary_length_avg":329.2,"title_length_avg":53.1,"title_length_var":304.39,"tag_entropy":2.834933,"tag_diversity":1.25,"top_tag_share":0.55,"avg_upvotes":0.55,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.1,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.25,"zero_engagement_share":0.55,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.159455,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.176471},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-5.6176,8.2353],"cadence_depth":[-8.2059,-6.2353],"hype_variety":[-7.8971,-3.6324],"title_style":[-7.9118,-4.7794]},"top_tags":[["rust",14],["webassembly",4],["fermyon",3],["webdev",3],["cloud",2],["azure",2],["career",2],["serverless",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Weekly Rust Trivia: How to Implement Binary Search","What I\u2019ve Been Up To \u00b7 Thorsten Hans","Wasm ahead - Joining Fermyon"],"outlier":["Azure Key Vault FlexVolume for Kubernetes \u2014 A journey to integrate Azure Key Vault and AKS"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"LFelxg7m6","title":"What I\u2019ve Been Up To \u00b7 Thorsten Hans","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/whats-ive-been-up-to/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-i-ve-been-up-to-thorsten-hans-lfelxg7m6","summary":"A curated collection of technical articles covering Spin framework development, including OpenAPI documentation generation, performance optimization with Wizer, custom template creation, routing solutions comparison, Kubernetes integration with SpinKube and KEDA, observability with OpenTelemetry, Azure deployments, and building serverless applications with HTMX. The posts explore WebAssembly workloads, security practices like SBOM generation, and practical implementations using Rust and JavaScript/TypeScript.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/30dec75819ec604d709e77293dc78010?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-16T14:50:52.855Z"},{"id":"S1ZmF6aTJ","title":"Azure DevOps Extensions for Spin, Fermyon Wasm Functions and Fermyon Cloud \u00b7 Thorsten Hans","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/azure-devops-extensions-for-spin-fc-and-fwf/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/azure-devops-extensions-for-spin-fermyon-wasm-functions-and-fermyon-cloud-thorsten-hans-s1zmf6atj","summary":"Three new Azure DevOps extensions enable building and deploying Spin applications directly from pipelines. The base Spin extension provides CLI installation, plugin management, and build capabilities. Two deployment-focused extensions target either Fermyon Wasm Functions (serverless, globally distributed) or Fermyon Cloud (managed platform). Each extension offers dedicated pipeline steps for authentication, deployment, and application management, replacing manual bash scripting with integrated Azure DevOps tasks that support variables, secrets, and conditional logic.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/30dec75819ec604d709e77293dc78010?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-16T14:50:52.689Z"},{"id":"tORXrOteg","title":"Uses \u00b7 Thorsten Hans","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/uses/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/uses-thorsten-hans-torxroteg","summary":"A curated list of hardware, software, and tools used by a professional software developer and consultant. The setup includes a MacBook Pro M3 Max as the primary machine, dual LG 4K monitors, and a ZSA Voyager keyboard. For software development, the author uses Visual Studio Code and neovim as editors with Monaspace Krypton or Dank Mono fonts, Ghostty terminal with tmux and oh-my-zsh, and Starship for the command prompt. The blog is built with Hugo, notes are managed in Notion, and tasks are tracked using Apple Reminders.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/30dec75819ec604d709e77293dc78010?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-10-16T14:50:52.651Z"},{"id":"OzyAxbCTN","title":"WebAssembly and Containers with Docker Desktop - Hello World and Beyond","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/webassembly-and-containers-with-docker-desktop-hello-world-and-beyond/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/webassembly-and-containers-with-docker-desktop---hello-world-and-beyond-ozyaxbctn","summary":"Explore how to run WebAssembly workloads in Docker Desktop to build distributed architectures.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7e4833e3fdd3e1146e0279deb5bc75cc?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-28T14:27:55.000Z"},{"id":"TuFljWpVQ","title":"Wasm ahead - Joining Fermyon","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/wasm-ahead-joining-fermyon/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/wasm-ahead---joining-fermyon-tufljwpvq","summary":"The author announces their joining of Fermyon as a Cloud Advocate and highlights Fermyon's vision for leading the era of cloud computing and their use of WebAssembly. They also mention the Spin project and Bartholomew as tools to simplify app development using Wasm.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6253790e883d414e2c27b6897168ab8a?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-08T11:05:52.000Z"},{"id":"RfRbrNDjw","title":"A Farewell to Thinktecture","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/farewell-to-thinktecture/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-farewell-to-thinktecture-rfrbrndjw","summary":"The author is saying goodbye to Thinktecture AG after almost nine years. They reflect on their time with the company and express gratitude for the experiences and growth opportunities. The author helped developer teams embrace new technologies and invites readers to stay connected through their blog and LinkedIn.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/55ef6a933210b68bf7e95599f37e1b00?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-20T11:23:44.000Z"},{"id":"cHyPX1pF2","title":"A comprehensive guide on authoring plugins for Fermyon Spin","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/comprehensive-guide-on-authoring-plugins-for-fermyon-spin/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-comprehensive-guide-on-authoring-plugins-for-fermyon-spin-chypx1pf2","summary":"A comprehensive guide on authoring plugins for Fermyon Spin is available to all users. In this article, we will explore how I build the plugin - a simple Spin plugin that allows you to check if your local installation of the CLI is outdated. We\u2019ll wrap up this article by adding the custom Spin plugin to the Spin Up Hub.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/aac4f481ed78f889f652e07597b87208?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-25T08:05:15.000Z"},{"id":"X3Rsh1Kpj","title":"Weekly Rust Trivia: How to use pattern matching","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/weekly-rust-trivia-pattern-matching/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/weekly-rust-trivia-how-to-use-pattern-matching-x3rsh1kpj","summary":"In Rust, pattern matching is a powerful language feature that allows you to destructure data and match it against specific patterns. It helps you handle different cases and extract values from complex data structures with concise and readable code. The wildcard pattern in Rust\u2019s pattern matching acts as a default case, handling unmatched situations.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/efa20cd985673d09003ef2b233159c0f?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-03T11:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"rfb8tjVfj","title":"Weekly Rust Trivia: How to share state between threads","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/weekly-rust-trivia-share-state-between-threads/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/weekly-rust-trivia-how-to-share-state-between-threads-rfb8tjvfj","summary":"In Rust, we have the ability to share data between threads by using concurrent data structures and synchronization tools provided by the Rust standard library. For demonstration purposes we\u2019ll use a simple vector ( ) and share it between multiple background threads. Each background thread will push data to the state in a controlled and safe manner.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4ac5018dd0177aad841bf84d7f58a429?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-27T11:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"iMZqjsT0Q","title":"Weekly Rust Trivia: How to write a function-like macro","url":"https://www.thorsten-hans.com/weekly-rust-trivia-function-like-macros/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/weekly-rust-trivia-how-to-write-a-function-like-macro-imzqjst0q","summary":"Function-like macros are defined using the keyword and a set of rules that define patterns and transformations. In Rust, we can use a function-like macro by invoking its name followed by an exclamation mark. The macro expands and generates code, which is then used in your program.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6fa58d641e04fbd57bd26a04986103ec?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-20T11:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["lisacrispin","matthiasnoback","aimodelsfyi","leaverou","visiblequality"],"opposite_handles":["alexfinn","tbpn","kloss_xyz","ryolu_","felixrieseberg"],"similar":[{"id":"lisacrispin","handle":"lisacrispin","name":"Agile Testing","is_squad":false,"x":-6.7971,"y":-3.5421,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected